{"duration_api_ms":201979,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"0204548c-a824-57b7-bea3-1783011bc81a","total_cost_usd":1.278457,"usage":{"input_tokens":64,"cache_creation_input_tokens":50191,"cache_read_input_tokens":2238865,"output_tokens":21445,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":5186},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":50191,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1184,"cache_read_input_tokens":95385,"cache_creation_input_tokens":860,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":860},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":64,"outputTokens":21445,"cacheReadInputTokens":2238865,"cacheCreationInputTokens":50191,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.278457,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":5186,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":50191,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":32,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I've finished PKT-0054. The time goes to measuring each cell's text, then to drawing. It is not page setup. Committed as `afa4d6a`.\n\n**Findings** (in `.theseus/diagnosis/PKT-0054-xlsx-pdf-layout.md`):\n- **Where it goes:** almost all of the layout phase is one call, `asc_nativeGetPDF`. In a CPU profile of a 25k-row sheet:\n  - 79% is building the text-metrics cache before drawing. Most of that is font shaping, done fresh for every cell with nothing reused. Number formatting (`Cell._getValue2`) is about 40% and overlaps with the shaping.\n  - Drawing (row backgrounds and cell text) is about 33%. These shares overlap, so they don't add to 100%.\n  - Page setup (`calcPagesPrint`) is about 3%, and turning on fit-to-width changed nothing (38.1 s vs 37.9 s).\n- **It scales linearly:** about 0.7 ms of CPU per row, or about 35 ms per printed page. Nothing grows faster per page. Text versus numbers makes no difference.\n- **Part of the 44 s is the sample file:** big-50k's formulas have no saved results, so x2t recalculates them all, which adds about 13–15 s. Real Excel files normally store those results.\n- **Only the active sheet is printed:** the file has 3 sheets but the PDF has 1,042 pages, all from sheet 1.\n\n**Decisions:**\n- I compared CPU time, not wall time. The VM is shared with other agents and the same file took anywhere from 50 to 85 s.\n- `perf` isn't installed, so I profiled through doctrenderer's built-in V8 inspector, turned on with `V8_USE_INSPECTOR=1`. The new tool is `x2t-cpuprofile.js`. The inspector only handles messages while V8 is paused, so the tool pauses before each script and makes `asc_nativeGetPDF` pause once it returns. Profiling slows runs by about 1.6×, so only the proportions count.\n- I also added `x2t-cpu.sh` (CPU, wall time and memory per conversion) and `xlsx-variants.py` (the test files above).\n\n**Not done:**\n- I changed nothing in sdkjs, because it is read-only under `external/`.\n- Each variant was run once.\n- I didn't profile the formula recalculation on its own.\n- The packet has no acceptance commands to run. `theseus validate` passed with 1 warning and 0 errors; I didn't check what the warning was.\n\n**Follow-up requested** in `.theseus/spawn/` (requires `documentserver`): prototype a text-shaping cache keyed by font, size and text in the xlsx print path, or skip measuring numbers that already fit. Then measure whether the saving is worth forking sdkjs.\n\n**Lessons for the Atlas:**\n- The xlsx → pdf cost is in `drawForPrint` → `_prepareCellTextMetricsCache` and grows linearly with rows.\n- doctrenderer has two debug switches: `V8_USE_INSPECTOR=1` opens a DevTools connection on port 8080 and waits for a client, and `js_speed=1` prints the time of each JS call.\n- On the shared factory VM, compare CPU time rather than wall time.\n\nThe executor log and the friction line are filled in.","ttft_ms":1827,"type":"result","duration_ms":1124395,"uuid":"448de1af-1a59-42f9-bd39-dcb4b9b44cf0","ttft_stream_ms":1036,"time_to_request_ms":445,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":13,"system_prompt":184,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":6,"input_attachments":30,"input_hooks":6,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":54,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":21,"init_frame_send":9,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":8,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":3,"request_announcements":23,"query_setup":11,"auto_mode_context_wait":15,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":34,"message_normalization":4,"client_creation":7,"request_build":13},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":149,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":200,"time_to_request_major_faults":1,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":214,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":139,"process_rss_mib_result":249,"process_anon_mib_result":166,"process_peak_rss_mib":262,"process_cpu_ms_turn":10094,"process_wall_ms_turn":1124395,"process_cpu_ms_streaming":2998,"process_wall_ms_streaming":180820,"main_stream_count":32,"main_stream_event_count":2716,"main_stream_chunk_count":2144,"input_attachments_detail":{"slowest_producer":"artifact_opening_prefetch","slowest_producer_ms":13,"cpu_ms":27,"major_faults":0,"setup_ms":0,"prompt_producers_ms":0,"ambient_start_ms":11,"ambient_wait_ms":13,"render_ms":2,"producers":41,"token_counts":0